            nothing graded
        
        --- INVARIANT ASSERTIONS DELIBERATELY EXEMPTED BY A VECTOR (the vector says why, here) ---
            An exemption is a check the VECTOR switched off, not one the harness could not run. It is
            admissible only for a shape where the REFERENCE ORACLE ITSELF violates the invariant and the
            implementation reproduces it, because there the assertion would be a claim about the oracle
            rather than about the port — and that is a graded-domain question, not a harness one. Every
            exemption below is named, scoped to one vector, and carries its own reason in full.
            THAT SENTENCE HAS TWO CONJUNCTS AND BOTH ARE NOW ASSERTED, in different places and with
            different consequences. (1) THE ORACLE CONJUNCT is decided OFFLINE, from the vector file
            alone, in the EXEMPTION GROUNDING section below: the exempted invariant is re-run against the
            schedule the CAPTURE recorded and must come back VIOLATED there, or the vector is refused.
            (2) THE PORT CONJUNCT is a statement about THIS RUN and is measured in the PORT CONJUNCT
            section below: the exempted invariant is run again, against the schedule THE IMPLEMENTATION
            RETURNED, and what it said is printed beside every exemption here. It is REPORTED, never
            refused — a port that satisfies an invariant the oracle violates has DIVERGED, and a
            divergence is the cell diff's finding, not a second admissibility verdict that could disagree
            with it. Until this run it was asserted by nothing, and the sentence above claimed it anyway.
            NONE — every invariant was asserted against every vector.
        
        --- EXEMPTION GROUNDING (every exemption re-run against the schedule ITS OWN VECTOR recorded) ---
            An exemption is admissible only where the REFERENCE ORACLE ITSELF violates the invariant. That
            is asserted, not assumed: each exempted invariant is re-run against the vector's own recorded
            schedule, honouring that vector's unrecorded_fields, and must come back VIOLATED there. This
            section reports the ORACLE conjunct only; whether the PORT reproduces the oracle's behaviour is
            a grading-time question and nothing here asserts it. Three verdicts are INADMISSIBLE, refused
            in Admit and never a warning: DECORATION (the invariant holds OUTRIGHT on the oracle's own
            numbers, with no assertion withheld, so the exemption silences nothing and only inflates the
            count above), NOT-EVALUABLE (the invariant has nothing to assert here at all, with nothing
            withdrawn) and SCHEDULE-UNREADABLE (the recorded rows do not parse into a schedule). A fourth,
            UNDETERMINED-ON-THE-RECORD, is REPORTED AND ADMITTED: this vector's own unrecorded_fields
            withdrew a cell the invariant reads, so the record is SILENT — which is not evidence against
            the exemption, and refusing it would kill a legitimate vector for a gap in the CAPTURE
            (finding T225-F1). It is counted apart from GROUNDED because it is not evidence either way.
            NIL-COVERAGE — no vector in this store exempts any invariant, so the exemption-grounding
            check inspected an empty population. It inspected 0 loaded vector(s) to find that out.
        
        --- EXEMPTION CITATIONS (which observation each admissible exemption rests on) ---
            An exemption's whole argument is that THE REFERENCE ORACLE WAS OBSERVED TO BEHAVE THIS WAY.
            Its `reason` is free prose and always was; until finding T222-F4 was closed, nothing required
            that prose to point at anything, so an OBSERVATION and an ASSERTION were indistinguishable to
            this harness. The citation is MINTED by the harness, not read from the vector, and it is
            refused in Admit unless all three components resolve: the committed capture ARTEFACT exists
            in this repository and is non-empty; the capture CASE ID occurs inside that artefact's bytes
            (a bundle citation that names no case in the bundle is a page that is not in the book); and
            the RECORD'S OWN SENTENCE — the exempted invariant re-run against the captured schedule — is
            non-empty. The byte offsets below are the proof the artefact was opened.
            NIL-COVERAGE — no vector in this store exempts any invariant, so no citation was required
            and none was minted. Stated rather than left as silence (P-35).
        
        --- PORT CONJUNCT (every exempted invariant re-run against the schedule THE IMPLEMENTATION RETURNED) ---
            The exemption sentence has two conjuncts: the oracle violates the invariant, AND the
            implementation reproduces it. The section above asserts the first, offline, and refuses when
            it fails. This asserts the second, on THIS run's output, and REPORTS rather than refuses: a
            port that SATISFIES an invariant the oracle violates has diverged from the oracle, which is a
            parity finding the cell diff owns. Nothing in this section can fail a vector, and nothing in
            it is a licence: DIVERGED here means the exemption is excusing a behaviour the port does not
            actually have, which is worth a reader's attention even when every graded cell matched.
            NIL-COVERAGE — no graded vector exempted any invariant on this run, so the port conjunct
            had an empty population. It is stated rather than left as silence.
        
        --- INVARIANT ASSERTIONS THAT COULD NOT RUN (a cell the capture never recorded) ---
            An invariant reads the schedule the implementation RETURNED. Where the implementation could not
            compute a cell — only the self-test replay ever can't, and only for a cell the vector's own
            unrecorded_fields withdrew — the assertions that read it are DECLARED not-applicable here rather
            than run against the stand-in. Both directions of that defect were live before this section
            existed: balance_roll_forward went RED on a placeholder, and principal_amortizes_to_zero went
            quietly GREEN on one, which is the worse half. A check that stops checking says so, in writing.
            NONE — every invariant assertion ran, on cells somebody actually observed.
        
